<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-DATA-08> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Redundancy, replication and idempotency" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-DATA-09> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#belongsToPolicyCategory> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#PolicyCategory_DATA> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-DATA-09> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#PolicyArtifact_POLICIES_REV_01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-DATA-09> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#hasPolicyStatement> "Transmission scheduling must prioritize critical data over secondary data using a generic criticality classification. Non-transmissible or redundant data must remain retained under the applicable policy and must not displace critical data from a limited transmission window." .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-DATA-09> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#hasPolicyType> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#ObligationPolicyType> .
