<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-02> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Explicit governance links" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-03> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#belongsToPolicyCategory> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#PolicyCategory_GOV> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-03> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#PolicyArtifact_POLICIES_REV_01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-03> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#hasPolicyStatement> "No action may be authorized if it exceeds any current constraint imposed by consent, the semantic contract, zone, security or resource capacity. When rules apply concurrently, final eligibility must correspond to their most restrictive intersection." .
