<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-04> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Policy determinism and versioning" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-05> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#belongsToPolicyCategory> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#PolicyCategory_GOV> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-05> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#PolicyArtifact_POLICIES_REV_01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-05> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#hasPolicyStatement> "Every state must be modeled as a first-class temporal entity. It must record `validFrom` upon creation and `validTo` only when it ends. A state derived from an observation must retain an explicit link to its source evidence. Planned expiration must not reuse `validTo` before effective closure." .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-05> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#hasPolicyType> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#ObligationPolicyType> .
