<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-22> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-03> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-22> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-GOV-04> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-22> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-ZONE-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-22> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#NonFunctionalRequirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-22> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#Requirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-22> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-22> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RNF-22" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RequirementsArtifact_Revised> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementIdentifier> "RNF-23" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementStatement> "The optional wellbeing module must permit a wearable subtype to specialize the existing Wearable class while retaining inherited user-device relations under RDFS reasoning. This is semantic extensibility; physical device drivers and sensor adapters are outside this release." .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-INT-02> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-VAL-05> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-INT-02> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#NonFunctionalRequirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#Requirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-23> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RNF-23" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RequirementsArtifact_Revised> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementIdentifier> "RNF-24" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementStatement> "Maintained ontology files must parse as Turtle/RDF and catalogue queries must execute using the supported SPARQL 1.1 features in RDFLib. OWL axioms are interpreted under each declared reasoner contract; no HTTP endpoint interoperability is claimed." .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-INT-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-VAL-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-INT-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-VAL-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#NonFunctionalRequirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#Requirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-24> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RNF-24" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RequirementsArtifact_Revised> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementIdentifier> "RNF-25" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementStatement> "The ontology must reuse standard vocabularies where applicable, including SOSA/SSN, SAREF, FOAF and GeoSPARQL, avoiding duplication of equivalent concepts without documented justification." .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-INT-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-VAL-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-INT-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#NonFunctionalRequirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#Requirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-25> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RNF-25" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RequirementsArtifact_Revised> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementIdentifier> "RNF-26" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementStatement> "The supported RDFS, HermiT, Openllet, JFact and Konclude adapters must expose their execution contracts and reject unavailable or unsupported native configurations without silently substituting another reasoner. This requirement concerns these adapters, not arbitrary external SPARQL services." .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-INT-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-VAL-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-INT-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-VAL-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#NonFunctionalRequirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#Requirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-26> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RNF-26" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#definedInArtifact> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RequirementsArtifact_Revised> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementIdentifier> "RNF-27" .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#requirementStatement> "Instrumentation must measure, at minimum, latency, energy consumption, model accuracy/quality, sleep/stress quality, migration cost, load, residual capacity and node trust during evaluation scenarios." .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-AUD-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-DATA-02> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-METRIC-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToMechanism> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#M-TIME-01> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-DATA-10> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-MODEL-08> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#tracedToPolicy> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#P-OPS-05> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#NonFunctionalRequirement> .
<http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#RNF-27> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/monitoringcontinuum#Requirement> .
